Subject: WebKit: compile the Curl NetworkCache::Data backend on PlayStation

NetworkCacheDataCurl.cpp defines the CURL NetworkCache::Data methods
(constructors, span, size, apply, subrange, concatenate, adoptMap,
tryCreateSharedMemory). The PlayStation port never listed it, because
NetworkCache::Data was unreferenced until ENABLE_CONTENT_EXTENSIONS pulled in
the content-rule-list store (API::createExtension calls
Data::tryCreateSharedMemory). Add it to WebKit_SOURCES, mirroring how GTK/WPE
compile NetworkCacheDataGLib.cpp. No symbol overlap with the common
NetworkCacheData.cpp (which only defines mapToFile/mapFile). Needed for the
ad blocker's WKContentRuleList on the PS5 build.

diff --git a/Source/WebKit/PlatformPlayStation.cmake b/Source/WebKit/PlatformPlayStation.cmake
--- a/Source/WebKit/PlatformPlayStation.cmake
+++ b/Source/WebKit/PlatformPlayStation.cmake
@@ -52,6 +52,12 @@ list(APPEND WebKit_SOURCES
 
     NetworkProcess/NetworkDataTaskDataURL.cpp
 
+    # Curl backend of NetworkCache::Data (ctors, span, tryCreateSharedMemory,
+    # ...). Unreferenced until ENABLE_CONTENT_EXTENSIONS pulled in the content
+    # rule list store (APIContentRuleListStore createExtension), so the port
+    # never compiled it; GTK/WPE compile the GLib variant the same way.
+    NetworkProcess/cache/NetworkCacheDataCurl.cpp
+
     NetworkProcess/Classifier/WebResourceLoadStatisticsStore.cpp
 
     Platform/IPC/unix/ArgumentCodersUnix.cpp
